1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:00,585
Achoo!

2
00:00:00,585 --> 00:00:03,877
A sneeze is your nose's built-in alarm and cleaning system.

3
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:09,986
Dust, pollen, pepper or a cold virus irritates the lining inside your nose.

4
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:15,154
Nerves in the nose send a signal to the sneeze center in your brainstem.

5
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:22,285
You breathe in deeply, then air bursts out through nose and mouth to flush the irritant away.

6
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:27,739
The droplets can fly far, and they carry germs to the people around you.

7
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:29,681
Step 1.

8
00:00:29,681 --> 00:00:33,133
Sneeze into a tissue or your elbow, not into your hands.

9
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:35,637
Step 2.

10
00:00:35,637 --> 00:00:39,069
Throw the tissue away and wash your hands with soap and water.
